  tags={["Python", "OpenGL"]}
  githubUrl="https://github.com/alyashour/Marching-Cube-Renderer"
>
  <p>
    An implementation of the marching cubes algorithm, which walks a 3D
    scalar field cube by cube and extracts a polygonal surface wherever it
    crosses a chosen threshold. The result is rendered in OpenGL.
  </p>
  <p>
    A classic technique for turning volumetric data — voxel grids, implicit
    functions, scan data — into a mesh a renderer can draw. Full source is on
    GitHub.
  </p>
</ProjectLayout>
